    "message": "feat(routing): show where images go, and give the vision adapter a chain\n\nThree gaps, all found by looking at the running dashboard rather than the code.\n\n**The routing page never mentioned images.** Each tier drew its fallback rail,\nwhich answers \"what covers this model when it fails\". It cannot answer \"what\nhappens to a screenshot\", because the vision adapter fires on what a request\n*contains* rather than on a failure -- so the adapter sat in an isolated card\nat the bottom of the page, disconnected from the tiers it actually affects. A\ntier whose model is documented not to read images was silently sending them\nelsewhere and nothing said so.\n\nA tier whose model is known blind now carries a hop under its rail:\n\n    IMAGES -> chatgpt_oauth/gpt-5.6-luna\n    nous_portal/tencent/hy3:free cannot read them\n\nIt appears only on tiers that need it, so its presence is the signal. With no\nadapter configured it turns amber and says the images will fail there. The\nadapter's own card names the tiers it covers today rather than restating the\nrule.\n\n**Most of the catalog had no vision metadata at all**, so that hop could not\nhave been drawn for anyone. models.dev enrichment was gated to Novita and\ncustom providers; every other provider fell back to whatever it published\nitself, which for ~30 of them is nothing. Enrichment now runs for every\nprovider. It only fills fields the provider left null, so a gateway that\npublishes its own modality data keeps it. Measured on this machine: 337 of 948\nmodels are now known to reject images, up from the handful the OpenRouter-\ndialect providers reported. `/admin/api/models` returns that set as\n`blind_models` -- only reported refusals, never silence.\n\n**The vision adapter had no fallbacks.** One unreachable vision model lost\nevery image on the machine. `MODEL_VISION_FALLBACKS` is the same\ncomma-separated form as the tier chains, validated by the same validators,\nedited by the same rail editor, and its providers are warmed by the same\n`configured_chat_model_refs` walk. A diverted request now runs the adapter's\nchain first, then whatever on the original route can still see. An entry known\nto reject images is dropped from a *vision* chain -- that is always a mistake,\nnot a preference.\n\nTracking comes free: the diverted chain is a chain, so `route_chain`,\n`route_attempt` and the `vision` diversion pair added in 4.42.0 already\ndescribe it end to end.\n\nAlso fixed: a diverted request read as \"Primary model\" in the request detail,\nwhich named the wrong decision entirely. It now says \"Vision adapter, instead\nof <route model>\".\n\nVerification, in a real browser against a real config:\n- The hop renders on Sonnet only -- the one tier whose model models.dev knows\n  is text-only -- and the adapter card reads \"Currently covers Sonnet\".\n- Adding a vision fallback lights Apply, writes `MODEL_VISION_FALLBACKS` to\n  `.env`, and survives a reload. The hidden chain input is in the document,\n  which is the 4.34.1 failure mode that made chains unsaveable.\n- Caught and fixed a real ordering bug this way: the routing section renders\n  from the config payload *before* the model catalog loads, so the first paint\n  had an empty blind-model set and drew nothing. The hops now update in place\n  when the catalog arrives, which also keeps unsaved edits.\n- Full suite 3351 passed, 6 failed (the PowerShell installer baseline).\n  ruff format, ruff check, ty clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
